        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan G. Hevesi, John Faso\n- Roles: New York City Comptroller, Assembly Minority Leader, U.S. Representative\n- Places: New York City, New York's 19th congressional district\n- Events: New York Comptroller election, 2002\n\nFacts:\n- In the 2002 New York Comptroller election, New York City Comptroller Alan G. Hevesi defeated former Assembly Minority Leader John Faso.\n- John James Faso Jr. was born on August 25, 1952.\n- Since January 3, 2017, John Faso has served as the U.S. Representative for New York's 19th congressional district.\n- New York's 19th congressional district is currently represented by Republican John Faso.",
